learnings:
  - Any id that reaches path.join must be validated at the lowest layer (loader/projector), not only in lint of the parsed meta — lint checked meta.id while the CLI argument drove the paths.
  - Self-attested content hashes are drift detection, not tamper evidence; tamper evidence requires something the tamperer cannot rewrite.
  - Splitting a Phase into core (mcp) + surface (CLI/seeds) builders with a written API contract avoided turn-limit truncation and allowed parallel fix passes.
  - integration-build.test rebuilds dist and flakes under concurrent vitest/CLI use.
